<title>FINLAND: Finnish Oct EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.3 pct -SF.</title>
<headline>Finnish Oct EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.3 pct -SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.3 percent year-on-year in October after a 1.2 percent rise in September, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>				Oct 1996	Sept 1996    Oct 1995</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+1.3 pct	 +1.2 pct    +0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    +0.2 pct	 +0.2 pct    +/-0 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)   102.5	    102.3	 101.1</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices rose 0.2 percent in October on September and rose 0.7 percent year-on-year, it said.</p>
<p>			     Oct 1996	 Sept 1996     Oct 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr		     +0.7 pct	  +0.5 pct	+0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		   +0.2 pct	  +0.2 pct	+/-0 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)  113.0	     112.8	   112.2</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 0.7 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.2 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
